{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our digoxin 0.25 mg/mL injection supply to a plant classified OAI 2,662 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E8", "D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Digoxin 0.25 mg/mL injection (NDC 00641141035) used at both Corvale sites is labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. and manufactured at Hikma Farmaceutica (Portugal) S.A., FEI 3002807173 [E15].",
      "cites": ["E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That plant received an OAI classification on 2014-03-28 (inspection 876911) and a Warning Letter on 2014-10-21 [E8, E14].",
      "cites": ["E8", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The OAI inspection ended 2,662 days before FDA first posted the digoxin shortage on 2021-06-04 [D6].",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent inspections of the same plant in 2015, 2016, 2020, 2023 (two) were all classified VAI [E9, E10, E11, E12, E13].",
      "cites": ["E9", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A second registered plant for digoxin tablets, Bryant Ranch Prepack (FEI 1000519407), had an OAI inspection ending 2009-06-11 and a Warning Letter on 2010-04-08, with later inspections VAI through 2026-07-16 [E17, E26, E18, E19, E20, E21, E22, E23, E24, E25].",
      "cites": ["E17", "E26", "E18", "E19", "E20", "E21", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage has been on FDA's list for 65 months as of 2026-10-21 [D11].",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 14.5 days of the 0.25 mg/mL injection and can transfer 6 units to Corvale East, which holds 6.1 days, raising East to 7 days [D1, D2, D12].",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D12"]
    }
  ]
}
